{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And HaShem spoke to Moses: Go, descend.</b> From the redundancy of expression, and furthermore because it was not said 'descend from the mountain,' the Sages (Berakhot 32a) learned to interpret it as 'descend from your greatness' — and this is by way of punishment, because he accepted the mixed multitude. This is what it says: 'for your people has become corrupt' (Exodus 32:7) and so on — 'they have turned aside quickly' (Exodus 32:8) and did not wait, and not even a day or two would they stand firm in their faithfulness, and not only that, but they also caused Israel to sin: 'and they said, these are your gods, O Israel' (Exodus 32:8). 'And HaShem said to Moses: I have seen this people' (Exodus 32:9) — this He said with reference to Israel, and because they corrupted their deeds He called them 'the people.' And He said: I have already seen, these many days, the stubbornness of their neck — for even in Egypt they were wicked and sinful, as is found in the prophecy of Ezekiel (Ezekiel 20), and now their measure has been filled; therefore 'leave Me alone' (Exodus 32:10) — that I shall no longer deal with them Myself; therefore He said 'to Me.' 'And My anger shall blaze against them' (Exodus 32:10) — for I shall send against them an embassy of angels of wrath and fury. 'And I shall consume them' (Exodus 32:10) — for the emissary is not merciful and will not bear their iniquity at all."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:24:50.027541360Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}